# Hebrew + English DOCX

## Where content lives

Save in the repo under `docs/` (or path the user gives):

- **`.md`** — tagged draft while writing; optional git mirror later
- **`.docx`** — Word deliverable to send; **canonical after first export**

| Stage | Save to | Tool |
|-------|---------|------|
| Drafting | `.md` | edit markdown |
| First export | `.md` → `.docx` | `md_to_rtl_docx.py` |
| Any later change | **`.docx`** (required) | `rtl_docx_tool.py` |
| Optional mirror | `.md` | manual sync only |

After `.docx` exists: always `extract` first (picks up Word edits), then `replace-paragraph` / `replace-section` on **that same `.docx` path**.

**Word edits are sacred:** never `md_to_rtl_docx.py --force` unless the user explicitly requests rebuild **and** accepts losing Word edits (`--discard-word-edits` required). Do not sync from stale `.md`.

What gets **sent** is the `.docx`. Do not send `.md` unless the user explicitly asks.

## Audience — recipient vs author (blocking)

Documents for an external reader (supervisor letter, committee response):

- **Never** add content the user wanted **in chat only** or marked «בשבילי לא בשביל [recipient]».
- **Never** add internal QA stats, UI verification instructions («בדוק שורה־שורה בממשק»), or author-team voice («למפות שלנו»).
- Write **to the recipient** at their level; keep dev/ops notes in chat.

## Never

- Full `md_to_rtl_docx.py` re-run on an existing doc (`--force --discard-word-edits` only if user explicitly requests rebuild and accepts losing Word edits)
- Edit content only in chat without writing to `.docx`
- Markdown tables (`|…|`) in Hebrew docx — use bullets instead
- Raw zipfile XML; one-run mixed Hebrew+English

Skill: `pipeline/.codex/skills/heb-en-docx/SKILL.md`
